course: dictionary
lesson: 679
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word ballet can name a kind of dance, one show, or a whole company of dancers. Read the words around it, then decide which meaning fits.
explain: «Ballet has many famous male dancers, such as Rudolf Nureyev and Mikhail Baryshnikov.» Here ballet means the dance itself, because the sentence talks about dancers and the skill they need. Ask yourself: what is this sentence about? That question points you to the right meaning.
explain: «The Nutcracker» and «Swan Lake» are a ballet, one show with a story. «The Royal Ballet» is a company, a group of dancers who perform together. Look for clues like show, story or company, and you will know which meaning the writer chose.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Ballet» can mean a kind of graceful dance, one show, or a company of ballet dancers.
fact: «Pirouette» means a fast turn on one foot, and «plié» means bending the knees.
fact: «En pointe» means dancing on the tips of the toes, in special stiff shoes.
fact: Ballet grew up at the French court, so many of its steps and words are French.
exercise: «Ballet has many famous male dancers, such as Rudolf Nureyev.» In this sentence, what does ballet mean? | *A kind of graceful dance | A pair of soft shoes | A school sports lesson | A town in France
exercise: Maya says, «We are going to see a ballet tonight.» What does ballet mean here? | A company of dancers | The shoes you wear for dance | A swimming lesson | *One show or story performed in this dance
exercise: Ellie says, «I go to ballet class after school.» What does ballet mean? | *A lesson in the dance called ballet | A famous castle in France | A play about the sea | A company that tours the world
test: «Ballet takes strength and practice, like sport.» What does ballet mean in this sentence? | A type of shoe | A famous show | *The dance itself | A company of dancers
test: Sam saw three ballets last year. What does ballets mean? | Dance steps | *Shows or stories performed in this dance | Ballet dancers | Tights
exam: Which clue in «The hardest dances, like ballet on the tips of the toes, need years of training» shows that ballet means the dance style? | The French court | *The tips of the toes and years of training for strength and balance | A famous show | The big squat-kicks of hopak
